--TEST--
A `covariant` parameter of a generator method is tested when the method is called, before it returns its iterator, and a value of the wider type throws a `LogicError` — for a plain, a variadic and a static parameter — `rule:classes/a-covariant-type-is-checked-where-a-value-enters`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Animal {}
class Dog extends Animal {
    public function name(): string { return "dog"; }
}
class Cat extends Animal {}

class Shelter {
    public function each(Animal $a): Iterator<string> { yield "animal"; }
    public function all(Animal ...$all): Iterator<string> {
        foreach ($all as Animal $a) {
            yield "animal";
        }
    }
    public static function one(Animal $a): Iterator<string> { yield "animal"; }
    public static function call(Animal $a): Iterator<string> { return static::one($a); }
}

class DogShelter extends Shelter {
    public function each(covariant Dog $a): Iterator<string> {
        yield $a->name();
        yield "again";
    }
    public function all(covariant Dog ...$all): Iterator<string> {
        foreach ($all as Dog $a) {
            yield $a->name();
        }
    }
    public static function one(covariant Dog $a): Iterator<string> { yield $a->name(); }
}

// A `Dog` runs the generator, and its body reads the parameter as a `Dog`.
Shelter $s = new DogShelter();
foreach ($s->each(new Dog()) as string $x) {
    echo $x, "\n";
}

// 1. A `Cat` through the parent's type throws at the call, before the first element.
try {
    Iterator<string> $it = $s->each(new Cat());
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "1: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 2. A variadic parameter tests each argument.
foreach ($s->all(new Dog(), new Dog()) as string $x) {
    echo $x, "\n";
}
try {
    foreach ($s->all(new Dog(), new Cat()) as string $x) {
        echo $x, "\n";
    }
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "2: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 3. A static method, called through `static::` in the parent.
try {
    foreach (DogShelter::call(new Cat()) as string $x) {
        echo $x, "\n";
    }
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "3: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// 4. A variadic generator without `covariant` receives every argument.
Shelter $plain = new Shelter();
foreach ($plain->all(new Cat(), new Dog()) as string $x) {
    echo $x, "\n";
}
// covers: lang:classes/covariant
--EXPECT--
dog
again
1: The parameter `$a` of `DogShelter::each` has the type `Dog`. The argument is an object of class `Cat`.
dog
dog
2: The parameter `$all` of `DogShelter::all` has the type `Dog`. One of the arguments is an object of class `Cat`.
3: The parameter `$a` of `DogShelter::one` has the type `Dog`. The argument is an object of class `Cat`.
animal
animal
